Wrote `app.py` (single file) in the workspace root. It matches every requirement:

- **Flask + SQLite**, notes stored in `notes.db` next to the script; table created via `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` at startup (`init_db()` runs on import).
- **GET `/`** — lists all note texts and includes a form posting to `/add` with an input named `text`.
- **POST `/add`** — reads form field `text`, inserts it, redirects 302 to `/`.
- **POST `/delete/<int:id>`** — deletes that id, redirects 302 to `/`.
- Each note renders as its text followed by a delete form (submit button) posting to `/delete/<id>`, wrapped in `<div id="note-N">` so the literal `note-N` string is on the page.
- Runs on **127.0.0.1:5099** only when executed directly (`if __name__ == "__main__"`).

No auth, no template directory, no extra files — and I did not run it.
